Figure 5, "Nano-11 enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens," demonstrates Nano-11's ability to boost antigen internalization by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Flow cytometry results show that while soluble ovalbumin (OVA) alone leads to modest cellular uptake, its adsorption to Nano-11 (Nano-11+OVA) dramatically increases the percentage of OVA-containing BMDCs and the intracellular amount of OVA per cell. This enhanced delivery is critical for initiating immune responses, highlighting Nano-11's efficacy as a vaccine delivery vehicle and adjuvant by facilitating efficient antigen presentation to dendritic cells.